            "title": "Turbo",
            "description": "<p>Exonetik Turbo is collaborating with various industry leaders to bring to market a highly efficient ceramic turbine that can replace metallic turbines by being more efficient; replace piston engines by bringing more reliability; and act as a range extender for electric aircraft. The combination of efficiency and power density is the key to reduce greenhouse emissions, while accessing your destination.<br /></p>",
            "link": {
                "url": "/contact-us",
                "title": "Contact us"
            }
        },
        "content": [
            {
                "contentPosition": "left",
                "content": "<p>Commercial turbines in the sub-megawatt range are more reliable and require less maintenance than Diesel engines. However, their poor thermal efficiency compared to Diesel engines (38% vs 45%) limits their marked penetration.<br /><br />Exonetik Turbo has invented an innovative patented architecture allowing up to 50% thermal efficiency and 5kW/kg power-density, where the standard metallic turbine is replaced with ceramics, allowing a resistance to foreign object damage and high temperatures.<br /></p>",
